PREDICATE VS NECESSARY OBSERVATION
Only the consumer-failure terminal predicate changes. It accepts original
producer statusnull/SIGTERM, or status1/signalnull with newly observed structured
EPIPE/write/errno-32 on this producer's actual stdout error object and matching
consumer-close context. Both paths require exact caller code/message, original
error-object forwarding, consumer status17, producer/consumer PID bindings,
producer exit/close before core settlement, pipe close after caller failure,
both PIDs absent and empty process group before harness settlement, bounded
elapsed time below45000ms, and no emergency/supervisor kill. Raw numeric/status
telemetry precedes verdict assertions. Missing evidence fails, never inferred
from an arbitrary stderr substring or relabeled structured evidence.

Observation additions apply ONLY to actual consumer-failure. The worker briefly
wraps child_process.spawn, forwards receiver/arguments/result unchanged, attaches
stdout-close and child-exit/close observers, and synchronizes builtin exports so
the byte-identical core uses that wrapper. It restores spawn at core rejection.
It does not intercept destroy/error/kill, attach a stdout error handler, change
signal disposition, swallow an error or add a second cleanup implementation.
Immediately before throwing at real chunk16, the worker durably records a
fresh random token, exact caller reason and both PIDs. A producer-only
uncaughtExceptionMonitor observes error fields and identity with the error seen
by stdout's non-handling events.errorMonitor, stdout descriptor1 and raw
destroyed/errored state, PID/PPID/token and that already-written caller
marker. It neither catches the exception nor sets exitCode. The existing v3
stdout write/drain and SIGTERM telemetry behavior is otherwise unchanged.
The structured observation is saved independently and in the producer receipt.
Worker event sequence independently proves local pipe close/child close/core
settlement order; no cross-process wall-clock ordering is presumed. EPIPE cause
is bound to the actual error object on the sole stdout pipe connected to this
failed consumer, not just a co-occurring error string. This is trusted fixture
instrumentation, not a defense against a malicious host forging every receipt.
The pinned runtime's stdout dummyDestroy resets stream state via _undestroy;
therefore errored/destroyed at uncaught observation are recorded, not assumed.
events.errorMonitor observes without consuming error or changing error handling.
Observation overhead is included in actual consumer memory, without subtraction.

